From 47d3376502966dfb27beb6910aadc713beec2fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:20:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] stats: include the isize 0 bin in the insert size
 standard deviation

The "insert size standard deviation" loop in output_stats() started at
isize 1, while the mean and the pair count over the same bins started at
0 and so included the isize 0 bin.  Pairs reported with TLEN 0 therefore
entered the denominator but not the sum of squares, and lowered the
standard deviation instead of raising it.  On the new test input (10 pairs,
two with TLEN 0, the rest 300 to 360) the old code reported an SD of 60.1
against a mean of 259.0; the correct value for that mean is 130.5.  The
loop now starts at 0, like the two loops before it.  The regression test
fails on the previous code.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
---
 NEWS.md                     |  5 +++++
 stats.c                     |  4 +++-
 test/stat/23.stats.expected |  2 ++
 test/stat/23_isize_zero.sam | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/test.pl                |  2 ++
 5 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 test/stat/23.stats.expected
 create mode 100644 test/stat/23_isize_zero.sam

diff --git a/NEWS.md b/NEWS.md
index 016ee0b..309e63c 100644
--- a/NEWS.md
+++ b/NEWS.md
@@ -34,6 +34,11 @@ Bug fixes:
   had flagged the supplementary records of duplicates.  Duplicates are now
   counted for the same records as `sequences`.
 
+* FIX.  `samtools stats` left the insert size 0 bin out of the sum of squares
+  for `insert size standard deviation` while including it in the mean and in
+  the denominator, so pairs reported with TLEN 0 lowered the standard
+  deviation instead of raising it.
+
 Release 1.24 (9th July 2026)
 ----------------------------
 
diff --git a/stats.c b/stats.c
index c69e558..3f88c35 100644
--- a/stats.c
+++ b/stats.c
@@ -1599,7 +1599,9 @@ void output_stats(FILE *to, stats_t *stats, int sparse)
         }
     }
     avg_isize /= nisize ? nisize : 1;
-    for (isize=1; isize<ibulk; isize++)
+    // Start at 0, as the mean and the denominator do: pairs in the isize 0
+    // bin must enter the sum of squares as well.
+    for (isize=0; isize<ibulk; isize++)
         sd_isize += (stats->isize->inward(stats->isize->data, isize) + stats->isize->outward(stats->isize->data, isize) +stats->isize->other(stats->isize->data, isize)) * (isize-avg_isize)*(isize-avg_isize) / (nisize ? nisize : 1);
     sd_isize = sqrt(sd_isize);
 
